# Cloudflare Pages path rules. First match wins, top to bottom.

/grid /arcade 301
/grid/* /arcade/:splat 301

# Run The Floor answers at /basketball too.
#
# The game lives at /hoops/ and stays there: that is the canonical link, it is
# what the share card pastes into a chat, and every script beside the page
# loads relative to it. This is a door with a name somebody can be handed,
# beside /baseball/, /football/ and /soccer/.
#
# IT IS A 302 AND THE RULES ABOVE ARE 301s, WHICH IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE
# BETWEEN A RENAME AND AN ALIAS. /grid became /arcade and is never coming
# back, so a browser is welcome to remember that for ever. This game is an
# unlaunched preview and where it finally lives is a decision nobody has made.
# A browser that cached a permanent redirect would go on answering /basketball
# out of its own cache, and nothing pushed to this site could change its mind.
#
# IT REDIRECTS RATHER THAN SERVING THE GAME IN PLACE, and that is deliberate.
# A 200 rewrite would keep /basketball in the address bar and would need the
# trailing slash to be right first: without it the page loads and every
# `engine.js?v=` beside it resolves against / instead, so the scripts 404 and
# the screen goes blank with nothing thrown. A redirect that does not fire is
# a 404 somebody reports. A rewrite that half fires is a white page.
#
# /baseball/ IS A REAL DIRECTORY HOLDING A DIFFERENT GAME. Nothing here may
# ever be written in a way that catches it.
/basketball /hoops/ 302
/basketball/* /hoops/:splat 302
